# Week 7 — Wireframes

## Journey
A volunteer finds an event and applies for a role.

## Screens
Screen | Purpose | Requirement 
1 Browse events | See events that need volunteers | FR08 
2 Event roles | See the roles of one event | FR08, FR10 
3 Apply for a role | Submit an application | FR09 
4 Missing information | Show what happens if a field is empty | Candidate 
5 Application sent | Confirm that the application was sent | FR09 

## Design notes
The screens use simple rectangles and text only. Data is fictional.
Screen 5 says "This is not a confirmed place", because the scenario does not say that an application is approved automatically.
Search, number of places and navigation are not shown, because they are not in the scenario.

## Candidate details (not confirmed)
Which event details are shown on Screen 1
Roles and required skills on Screen 2 (examples only)
Fields in the application form on Screen 3
The error message on Screen 4
Contact details and notifications

## Open questions
Can a volunteer apply for several roles in the same event?
How does the volunteer learn the decision?
How are skills or experience checked?

## Findings from review
Type of review: (self-review or peer-simulated)

Finding / Evidence type / Next step 
On Screen 2 it is not clear who checks the skills for a role.	Self-review	Ask Event Organiser how skills are checked.
on Screen 4 the error message is a proposed rule, not an agreed one.	Candidate rule	Ask Event Organiser if the field must be filled.
On Screen 5 the volunteer does not know how to learn the decision.	Self-review	Ask Event Organiser how volunteers are told.

Note: This review is not stakeholder validation
